  "interpretation": "<p>1.Auto Immune reactivity are not by themselves diagnostic and must be correlated with other laboratory and clinical&nbsp;findings.<br>2.Test conducted on Serum</p>\n<p><strong>Comments</strong></p>\n<p>Aquaporin 4 is a water channel protein involved in the regulation of water and electrolyte balance in the Central Nervous&nbsp;System. Neuromyelitis Optica is an inflammatory autoimmune disease causing demyelination of the central nervous system&nbsp;with degradation of the insulating sheath of at least one optical nerve (Neuritis nervi optici) and at the same time or few&nbsp;months later the spinal cord (Myelitis). Highly specific serum autoantibody markers are found very frequently in NMO, while&nbsp;they are not detected in multiple sclerosis (MS) or healthy subjects.</p>",
